{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1270466-artifacts-imbued-items-enhanced-items-and-grimoires","id":1270466,"title":"Artifacts, Imbued Items, Enhanced Items, and Grimoires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-24T17:47:03-08:00","id":1270466,"title":"Artifacts, Imbued Items, Enhanced Items, and Grimoires","content":"My best friend and I are having trouble understanding Artifacts, Imbued Items, Enhanced Items, and Grimoires and steps on how to create them and use them. I looked at the Homebrew list in the other threads, but they don't seem to be helping.<br /> <br /> What I know for sure is that Artifacts are from Supernal Realm, Imbued Items are stored spells created by Mages, Enhanced Items are regular items powered up, and Grimoires have spells and rotes we learn from them.<br /> <br /> I would appreciate it if someone can explain how those items are created with examples. Nothing overpowered, just simple ones. Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22337-overcastghost","name":"OvercastGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22337_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T18:02:12-08:00","id":1270471,"title":"","content":"Regular Mages don\u2019t make artifacts.<br /> <br /> Whenever you cast a spell on an item, like Crucible from Matter 3 you\u2019re creating an Enhanced Item.<br /> <br /> Whenever you write a Rote down with Scribe Grimoire at Prime 1 you\u2019re creating a grimoire.<br /> <br /> Whenever you imbue a Spell into an item using the rules for Imbue Item you\u2019re creating an imbued item. It could for instance be a wand that allows you to cast fireballs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T06:50:39-08:00","id":1270588,"title":"","content":"The rules for some of these (Artifacts, Imbued Items, and/or Enhanced Items, I don't remember which ones) will be updated in the upcoming book Signs of Sorcery because the rules from the core book are too unclear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T09:30:26-08:00","id":1272853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1270466-artifacts-imbued-items-enhanced-items-and-grimoires?p=1270471#post1270471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regular Mages don\u2019t make artifacts.<br /> <br /> Whenever you cast a spell on an item, like Crucible from Matter 3 you\u2019re creating an Enhanced Item.<br /> <br /> Whenever you write a Rote down with Scribe Grimoire at Prime 1 you\u2019re creating a grimoire.<br /> <br /> Whenever you imbue a Spell into an item using the rules for Imbue Item you\u2019re creating an imbued item. It could for instance be a wand that allows you to cast fireballs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Comes with a side of debilitating Paradox. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, his summation is accurate. Even the Seers get their Artifacts from Supernal sources (or digging them up from where Exarchs whispered they might be located). The only way of getting new ones brought down would be to summon a Supernal entity and get it to bring one with it, which shouldn't be easy.<br /> <br /> I'm glad to hear that they are getting updates in Signs of Sorcery, just one more reason to look forward to that book. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23958-tengugrib","name":"TenguGrib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T02:46:03-08:00","id":1272947,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly it is Grimoires that are getting an update.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-05T03:57:44-08:00","id":1272956,"title":"","content":"Grimoires will get expanded materials (primarily in new spells for making Grimoires out of weird things) but no rewrite. Doesn't really need it since they work as written and are not that confusing. It's imbued items that will get an update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-06T10:33:58-08:00","id":1273112,"title":"","content":"The distinction is quite simple:<br /> <br /> Enhanced items have had spells cast upon them.<br /> <br /> Imbued items cast spells when certain conditions are met.<br /> <br /> An item can be both enhanced and imbued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}